cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Eligibility dynamics in cross-sectional HIV incidence estimation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Demidont
    given-names: A. C.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9216-8569"
    affiliation: "Nyx Dynamics LLC"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nyx-Dynamics/nyx-eligibility-dynamics"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a methods paper on eligibility dynamics in
  cross-sectional HIV incidence estimation from recency assays. Establishes that
  transient movement into and out of unobservable states does not bias the
  estimator under stated stationarity and state-invariance conditions, and
  characterises the mechanisms that break that cancellation. Supersedes the
  analysis in Nyx-Dynamics/nyx-kassanjee-letter (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.20344293).
keywords:
  - HIV incidence
  - recency testing algorithm
  - cross-sectional incidence estimation
  - eligibility dynamics
  - counterfactual placebo
